# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 016
# Act: CON+  (Connection aimed at Figure)   Stance: Binding   Site: Link
#
# CON's second use: the actual relationships, drawn on specific entities.
# Two, independently: turn-12's anchor (signal-a) bound to side_a of
# turn-10's partition; turn-13's anchor (signal-b) bound to the same side.
# Neither binding depends on the other holding — each is checked against
# turn-10's partition and the respective entity's own anchor directly.
#
# This is the material CON* will need: two INDEPENDENT instances of the
# same kind of relationship (entity → side_a), not one relationship
# asserted twice about the same entity. That is exactly what was missing
# at gap-002, gap-008, and gap-011's first attempts, and exactly what is
# available here without construction — turn-12 and turn-13 already exist
# as two separate entities.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-15 (a relational field) and
# turn-12/turn-13 (entities to relate) and turn-10 (a side to relate them
# to). Refuted if either anchor's target were not actually a member of
# side_a per turn-10's own partition — checked: turn-10 names
# kernel/data/signal-a.json and signal-b.json as side_a; turn-12 and
# turn-13 anchor exactly those two files, respectively. Matches.

:turn-16  eot:opens        :turn-15 .
:turn-16  eot:act          eot:CON+ .
:turn-16  eot:stance       "Binding" .
:turn-16  eot:site         "Link" .
:turn-16  eot:binds        [ eot:entity "@f1292533ea4f49108d50bb02e4f2b56e5f62bbdd0686ad9728739b7c2c8aec3e" ; eot:to_side "side_a" ] .
:turn-16  eot:binds        [ eot:entity "@14ba529c7c6548b018aa4302dac0e84c97102ee043b421db4c734c3daec2d0d6" ; eot:to_side "side_a" ] .
:turn-16  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
